Trilogy of Terror is a 1975 American made-for-television anthology
horror film directed by Dan Curtis and starring Karen Black.

11
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
It features three segments, each based on unrelated
short stories by Richard Matheson.

12
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:14,571
The first follows a college professor who seeks excitement with her students;
the second is about twin sisters who have a bizarre relationship.

13
00:44:34,285 --> 00:44:40,285
These two segments were adapted by William F.

14
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
The third, adapted by Matheson himself, focuses on a woman
terrorized by a Zuni fetish doll in her apartment.

15
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
Black stars in all three segments, and plays dual roles in the second.

16
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
The film was first aired as an ABC Movie of the Week on March 4, 1975.

17
00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
Black initially turned down the project, but reconsidered when her
then-husband, Robert Burton, was cast in the first segment "Julie".

18
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
A television film sequel titled Trilogy of Terror II, written and
also directed by Dan Curtis, was released in 1996.

19
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
The film explores themes of seduction, sister,
anthology, evil doll, horror anthology.

